Day 303/350: Equal Sum Grid Partition I

Problem Statement #3564

Problem Statement Explantion:

Given an m×n integer grid, determine if it is possible to make exactly one horizontal or vertical cut such that the grid is divided into two non-empty rectangular sections with an equal sum of elements.
A horizontal cut is made between two adjacent rows.
A vertical cut is made between two adjacent columns.
The resulting two sections must both contain at least one cell. 

Solution Approach:

To solve this efficiently, we use the property that if a grid can be split into two equal parts, the sum of one part must be exactly half of the total sum of the grid.

1. Calculate Total Sum
First, we traverse the entire grid to find the totalSum. 
If totalSum is odd, it is mathematically impossible to split it into two equal integer sums, so we return false.

2. Check Horizontal Cuts
We iterate through the rows one by one (from the first row to the second-to-last row). 
We accumulate the sum of all elements in the current row into a horizontalPrefixSum. 
After processing each row, we check:

Does horizontalPrefixSum == totalSum / 2?
If yes, a valid horizontal partition exists.

3. Check Vertical Cuts
If no horizontal cut is found, we repeat the logic for columns. 
We iterate through columns (from the first to the second-to-last), accumulating the sum of all elements in the current column into a verticalPrefixSum.
Does verticalPrefixSum == totalSum / 2?
If yes, a valid vertical partition exists.

Here's the Code:

class Solution {
    public boolean canPartitionGrid(int[][] grid) {
        int m = grid.length;
        int n = grid[0].length;
        long totalSum = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
                totalSum += grid[i][j];
            }
        }

        if (totalSum % 2 != 0) {
            return false;
        }

        long target = totalSum / 2;

        long horizontalPrefixSum = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < m - 1; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
                horizontalPrefixSum += grid[i][j];
            }
            if (horizontalPrefixSum == target) {
                return true;
            }
        }

        long verticalPrefixSum = 0;
        for (int j = 0; j < n - 1; j++) {
            for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {
                verticalPrefixSum += grid[i][j];
            }
            if (verticalPrefixSum == target) {
                return true;
            }
        }

        return false;
    }
}

Complexity:

Time Complexity: O(m×n)
Space Complexity: O(1)





